### 11. **Important Implementation Details**

**Expiration Handling:**
- Incoming calls have a maximum ring time (typically based on MSC4075 spec)
- If user doesn't answer within this time, call is marked `.unanswered`
- Expiration is validated both in NSE (15 seconds) and main app

**CallKit Workaround:**
- After user answers, the code immediately ends the CallKit call (1 second delay)
- This is a workaround for an iOS bug with WKWebView/WebRTC/AVAudioSession
- The actual call is set up fresh in `setupCallSession()` without CallKit

**Sync on VoIP Push:**
- VoIP pushes don't trigger normal app state transitions
- App manually starts sync when `receivedIncomingCallRequest` action fires
- Uses background task to keep sync running briefly

**NSE Decryption:**
- NSE has full access to encrypted notifications via keychain
- Shares keychain with main app via app groups
- Can decrypt using stored session credentials

This is a sophisticated implementation that handles the complexity of end-to-end encrypted VoIP calls while respecting iOS background limitations!
